{
  "reason": "CausalBlock.forward applies padding masking only after attention, allowing left-padding keys to absorb attention probability from valid queries. The current macro validation HR@10 of 0.4813 versus baseline 0.505 motivates this controlled correction but does not establish causality. Historical sampled-softmax successes support preserving the objective, while failed retrieval and recency-weighting experiments support avoiding additional architectural or loss changes. Select model_design for the mask correction and training_evaluation to ensure the generated predictor uses identical masking.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Change only the attention mask in CausalBlock.forward(self, x, mask), preserving its signature, existing variable names, projections, residuals, dropout, and final return x * mask. Derive valid = mask.squeeze(-1).bool() and a lower-triangular causal matrix on x.device; construct allowed query-key pairs as (valid[:, :, None] & valid[:, None, :] & causal) | (~valid[:, :, None] & identity), then expand to shape [b, 1, t, t]. Pass this Boolean allowed mask as attn_mask to F.scaled_dot_product_attention with is_causal=False, remembering that True means allowed for this API; valid queries thereby attend only to nonpadding keys at their own or earlier positions, while padding queries attend only to themselves and are subsequently zeroed. This isolates padding dilution without introducing the learned retrieval or temporal reweighting changes associated with unsuccessful historical experiments. Keep SASRec signatures, dimensions, blocks, heads, embeddings, learned item bias, sampled-softmax objective, NEGATIVES=2048, TOKEN_CAP=2048, token quotas, and endpoint weighting unchanged.",
    "training_evaluation": "Ensure write_predict_script generates working/predict.py that imports the revised SASRec and CausalBlock from this trial's train.py, preserving write_predict_script, train_one, evaluate, validation_bank, predict, checkpoint configuration, and state-dictionary interfaces; retain the existing dynamic-import mechanism rather than duplicating the architecture. Include a lightweight deterministic mask check covering left-padded, unpadded, and entirely padded inputs: valid queries must exclude padding and future keys, padding rows must allow only their diagonal, and outputs must remain finite with padded outputs zero. Explicitly keep preprocessing seed 0, training and evaluation seed 42, supplied splits, prefix sampling, optimizer, learning rate and warmup, dropout, batch size, steps, environment-controlled SASREC_EPOCHS default 200, runtime limits, early stopping, and HR@10 checkpoint selection with NDCG tie-breaking unchanged. Retain all four dataset routes, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, single-GPU execution within the shared search budget, and exactly one newly trained selected checkpoint per category, without ensembles, checkpoint averaging, separate fitted scores, external data or weights, hidden-test access, or other-trial checkpoint reuse. Assess the hypothesized improvement over 0.4813 through the unchanged authoritative host macro validation HR@10 using 200 users per category and 99 unique negatives, without treating historical gains as evidence that this correction will improve performance."
  }
}
